          return _download_knowledge_blob(kr["gcsUri"]), f"gcs:{kr['gcsUri']}"

  If the local root exists but a file is absent, the function returns early and
  never attempts GCS — even though the blob is there.

  Verified consequence on 2026-10-04:
    06-Tool-Execution-Contract.md   -> ABSENT locally, never fetched from GCS
    07-Live-Diagnostics-Contract.md -> ABSENT locally, never fetched from GCS

  Both are listed in _KNOWLEDGE_RESOURCES, so the agent believes it has its
  safety contract and does not. The most safety-relevant artifact in the pack is
  the one that silently fails to load.

REPAIR
  Attempt GCS when the local read misses. The local directory's existence must
  not decide whether the cloud is consulted.

