FIX D7 — subprocess.run with shell=True and a list argument
================================================================================

PROBLEM
  agent.py:126-140

      subprocess.run([KNOUX_GCLOUD_PATH, "auth", "print-identity-token", ...],
                     shell=True, ...)

  With shell=True on Windows the list is joined into a single command line for
  cmd.exe without correct quoting. It happens to work today because the gcloud
  path contains no spaces — which is exactly the kind of latent failure that
  appears after someone installs to a path like C:\Program Files\Google Cloud SDK.

REPAIR
  Drop shell=True so the argument vector is passed to CreateProcess directly.

